    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (69.26) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (67.68) anchoring the lineup, representing our highest efficiency plays. **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** benefits from a favorable matchup against Scott, where the dynamic platoon advantage provides a significant +14% lift to his output. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** is positioned for a strong day against the lefty Weathers; despite a sub-elite SP_xERA, his elite xwOBA (0.377) and favorable park factors make him a cornerstone of our offensive strategy. **Josh Jung** (66.28) also warrants high confidence assuming he secures the #3 spot, as the combination of a soft matchup against Quintana and beneficial park factors elevates his projection despite the neutral platoon stance.\n\nRegarding bench construction, **Nolan Schanuel** (49.01) was the most difficult exclusion. While his projected efficiency is respectable, he ultimately fell short of the threshold required to displace our primary outfielders, as the higher variance and potential for stolen base accumulation from players like **Josh Lowe** and **Jackson Merrill** offer a superior aggregate path to category wins. We are monitoring the status of **Josh Jung**, whose score is contingent on confirmed placement in the #3 hole. Furthermore, while **Gunnar Henderson** faces a tough test against McClanahan, his score remains buoyed by the potential for stolen bases against a pitcher with a historically slow delivery\u2014a critical factor given our priority on speed. Managers should proceed with caution regarding **Josh Lowe** and **Andy Pages**, as both face \"Elite Hold\" catchers and pitchers, which historically suppress our stolen base opportunities despite their solid base projections.",
